<!--
  CLI Documentation — GraphCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.GraphCommand
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:cli="org.blockml.bml.cli"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:cliconfig="org.blockml.bml.cli.config"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:runtime="org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime"
  xmlns:framework="org.blockml.bml.framework"
  xmlns:graph="org.blockml.bml.graph"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>GraphCommand</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:GraphCommand</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>blockml graph specification</is>

  <documentation><![CDATA[Syntax:
    blockml graph index [--force] [--src dir] [--libraries a,b]
    blockml graph neighbors|uses|used-by FQN [--json] [--depth n] [--origin o] [--relation r] [--limit n]
    blockml graph ancestors|descendants|members FQN [--json] [--depth n]
    blockml graph path FROM TO [--json] [--depth n]
    blockml graph query CYPHER [--json]
    blockml graph schema [--json]

    Graph uses the same corpus as validate --all (@blockml/graph / bootstrapFullProjectRegistry).
    Missing or stale .blockml/graph/ is rebuilt automatically before a query.
    Unknown Block FQN → exit 2 (same as inspect); may print Did you mean …? when search finds a matching last segment, or when the token is a .bml path whose document-root FQN is in the corpus. Existing block with no hits → No matches / No path, exit 0.
    path follows outgoing authored edges only (same direction as uses); hops print --RELATION--> . Reverse questions use used-by.
    uses, used-by, and neighbors --depth n walks n hops (default 1). ancestors, descendants, and path use --depth as max hops (default 16). members ignores --depth.
    --origin workspace|dependency|unresolved and --relation BASE_TYPE|MEMBER_TYPE|… (comma-separated) filter uses/used-by/neighbors; --limit caps the list after those filters.
    graph schema names the Ladybug Cypher subset and prints a working MATCH example. No type() or shortestPath().
    --help and -h print the Printed help page and exit 0.
    The graph database is exclusive; the CLI waits if another graph process holds the index.
    --json prints the corresponding Graph API objects.
    Human lines: relation, FQN, relative file path and line.

Printed help:
Usage: blockml graph index [--force] [--src dir] [--libraries a,b]
       blockml graph neighbors|uses|used-by <fqn> [--json] [--depth n] [--origin o] [--relation r] [--limit n]
       blockml graph ancestors|descendants|members <fqn> [--json] [--depth n]
       blockml graph path <from> <to> [--json] [--depth n]
       blockml graph query <cypher> [--json]
       blockml graph schema [--json]
       blockml graph --help

When: inheritance, uses / used-by, members, or paths.

Prefer named operations. Use graph schema before Cypher.
Rebuild with graph index if the index is missing or stale.
Unknown FQN exits 2 (same as inspect). May print Did you mean …?
path follows outgoing authored edges only (the same direction as uses); reverse questions use used-by.
The graph database is exclusive; the CLI waits if another graph process holds the index.

Flags:
  --depth n     uses / used-by / neighbors: hops (default 1). ancestors / descendants / path: max hops (default 16). members ignores --depth.
  --origin      workspace|dependency|unresolved (comma-separated); uses/used-by/neighbors only
  --relation    BASE_TYPE|MEMBER_TYPE|… (comma-separated); uses/used-by/neighbors only
  --limit n     cap the list after origin/relation filters (uses/used-by/neighbors)
  --json        machine-readable Graph API objects
  --force       full rebuild for graph index
  --src / --libraries   corpus overrides

graph schema names the Ladybug Cypher subset (no type(), no shortestPath()) and prints a working MATCH example.

Related: search, inspect.]]></documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:RunGraph" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>

</block>
